post_install() {
  # NetworkManager reads conf.d only at startup or on a reload, so keeping
  # awdl0 and mon0 unmanaged isn't in force until something rereads it.
  # `reload conf` touches no connection.
  if systemctl is-active --quiet NetworkManager 2>/dev/null; then
    nmcli general reload conf >/dev/null 2>&1 \
      || echo "  Could not reload NetworkManager's configuration. Run: sudo nmcli general reload conf"
  fi
  cat <<'MSG'
  omdrop-owl is omdrop's radio half for MediaTek MT7925 Wi-Fi. Nothing runs
  until omdrop asks. The interface is the omdrop plugin, in a version that
  supports radio backends (docs/radio-backend.md):

      omarchy plugin add <omdrop plugin repository>
      omarchy plugin enable netmojo.omdrop

  Then turn omdrop on from its icon in the bar.

  Your Wi-Fi access point has to be on channel 6, 44 or 149: AirDrop shares
  its channel. `/usr/lib/omdrop/omdrop-discoverable probe` says what, if
  anything, is in the way.
MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}

pre_remove() {
  # Don't leave a window running on a helper that's about to disappear.
  /usr/lib/omdrop/omdrop-discoverable stop >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
}
